<title>GREECE: ATHLETICS-S.AFRICA'S CORBETT WINS WORLD MEN'S JAVELIN TITLE.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-S.AFRICA'S CORBETT WINS WORLD MEN'S JAVELIN TITLE.</headline>
<text>
<p>ATHENS, Aug 5 (Reuter) South African Marius Corbett won the</p>
<p>world men's javelin gold medal on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Steve Backley of Britain took the silver and Greek Kostas</p>
<p>Gatzioudis the bronze.    </p>
<p>Javelin final:</p>
<p> 1. Marius Corbett (South Africa) 88.40 metres</p>
<p> 2. Steve Backley (Britain)	 86.80</p>
<p> 3. Kostas Gatzioudis (Greece)    86.64</p>
<p> 4. Mick Hill (Britain)	     86.54</p>
<p> 5. Sergei Makarov (Russia)	 86.32</p>
<p> 6. Boris Henry (Germany)	   84.54</p>
<p> 7. Emeterio Gonzalez (Cuba)	83.56</p>
<p> 8. Aki Parviainen (Finland)	82.80</p>
<p> 9. Jan Zelezny (Czech Republic)  82.04</p>
<p> 10. Gregor Hogler (Austria)	81.56</p>
<p> 11. Andrei Moruyev (Russia)	81.38</p>
<p> 12. Patrik Boden (Sweden)	  80.66</p>
